  triage:title "Shared worker-pool logic not factored into generic constructor" ;
  triage:description "Shared worker-pool logic across the connection-admission strategies (ConnectionWorkerPool at local_ipc_transport/connection_workers.rs:45+ and DispatchWorkerPool at local_ipc_transport/request_worker.rs:64+) is not factored into a generic/shared constructor. Both implement nearly identical thread-pool initialization patterns with bounded admission queues. Arch-ctm confirmed (2026-08-03T02:09:03Z) this is real duplication and separate from connection-admission refactor, but deferred to same 'local-HTTP admission-consolidation' tracking (not in scope for current branch fix/localipcwake-accept-interrupt). No files changed on this branch." ;
